@startuml upload-flow
' Render (from docs/diagrams):
'   docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/data" -w /data plantuml/plantuml -tsvg upload-flow.puml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam titleFontSize 18
skinparam titleFontStyle bold
skinparam ArrowColor #222222
skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor #8A8A99
  TitleFontStyle bold
  TitleFontSize 14
}
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #EBEBF3
  BorderColor #6B6B7B
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  DiamondBorderColor #6B6B7B
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF2A8
  BorderColor #D4B000
  FontSize 12
}

title Flow: Processing a Newly Uploaded Video

|#F4F4F8|Browser|
start
:Person clicks **Add clip**,
picks a video, types title / language;
:POST /upload (form: file + metadata);

|#FFFFFF|API (api.py)|
if (extension in .mp4 .mov .webm .mkv .m4v?) then (no)
  :400 "unsupported file type";
  |Browser|
  :Show the error;
  stop
else (yes)
endif
|API (api.py)|
:Write sidecar **<name>.json**
(title, caption, language, people ...);
note right
  **api.py · upload()**
  Sidecar first, video last: the worker only
  looks for videos, so it never picks up a clip
  whose metadata has not landed yet.
end note
:Stream video to **<name>.mp4.part**,
then rename to <name>.mp4;
:Return {queued_as: <name>.mp4};
|Browser|
:Show "Queued";

|#F4F4F8|Worker (worker.py)|
:Wake up every 3 s (POLL_SECONDS);
:Sync gallery if a photo changed;
:pending(): videos in data/inbox
untouched for > 2 s, oldest first;
note right
  The 2 s rule skips files still being
  copied in by Finder or the browser.
end note

|#FFFFFF|Pipeline (pipeline.py)|
:load_meta(sidecar)
→ title, language, hashtags, people, topics;
:ffprobe → duration, size, has_audio;
if (duration > 30 s?) then (yes)
  :raise Rejected;
  |Worker (worker.py)|
  :Move to **data/failed**
  + <name>.error.txt;
  stop
else (no)
endif
|Pipeline (pipeline.py)|
:SHA-256 of the file;
if (same SHA already stored?) then (yes)
  :merge_duplicate():
  duplicates_seen + 1,
  new title kept as a name;
  |Worker (worker.py)|
  :Move to **data/processed**;
  stop
else (no)
endif
|Pipeline (pipeline.py)|
:4 keyframes + 64-bit picture hash each;
if (picture hashes close to a stored clip?) then (yes)
  :merge_duplicate()
  (re-encode or resize of a known clip);
  |Worker (worker.py)|
  :Move to **data/processed**;
  stop
else (no)
endif

|Pipeline (pipeline.py)|
:Web copy + thumbnail
→ media/<sha16>.mp4 / .jpg;

|#F4F4F8|Models|
if (has audio?) then (yes)
  :**Whisper** (stt.py): speech to text
  → Devanagari + Roman transcript;
  note right
    low_stt_confidence when
    avg_logprob < -1.0 or
    language probability < 0.5
  end note
else (no)
  :no_speech flag;
endif

|#FFFFFF|Postgres|
:INSERT clip (facts so far) → clip_id;

|#F4F4F8|Models|
:**InsightFace** (faces.py): faces on keyframes,
match against data/gallery;
note right
  Named at cosine >= 0.42.
  Flags: unknown_faces, weak_face_match.
end note
if (Laya reachable?) then (yes)
  :**Laya**: topic + mood choices,
  on title + dialogue and on title alone;
  note right
    Topic kept at >= 0.45 in either reading,
    after any sidecar topics.
  end note
else (no)
  :laya_failed flag;
endif
:**Mood** (vibe.py): FER+ on faces,
CLIP on keyframes, Laya text mood
→ reactions, use_when, description;

|Postgres|
:UPDATE topics, mood, people,
review flags, raw scores;
:**Index** (indexing.py): s_names, s_said,
s_people, s_meta + 384-number embedding;
note right
  Same normalise() the search query
  goes through, so spellings meet.
end note

|Worker (worker.py)|
:Move original to **data/processed**;
:Log "<name> -> new, clip_id, review reasons";

|Browser|
:Clip shows in search and trending,
with its share link /c/<id>;
stop

@enduml
